# refuse prose/en/wire/canonical · REFUSE·authority lane-A does not cover prose/en/wire/canonical
bound-lock/1 about="The canonical line is the header, then every field in the byte order of its key, one space apart, each value quoted only where it must be. Parsing a canonical line and writing it again gives back the same bytes. The digest of a line is the {hash} of those bytes, and a signature travels beside the bytes it signs, never inside them." at=policy:wire-page by=lane-A epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/wire/canonical sig="ed25519:era1:HBBQsGfqgutC5uqUl7za3efPjixVjjaT0IFaou6vyyBSEU8WTTctgJbu+dqXnEJNeVTFNJZEqqEM84KmaKBwAA==" value=lock
