# refuse prose/en/wire/values · REFUSE·authority lane-A does not cover prose/en/wire/values
bound-lock/1 about="The kernel never looks inside a value; each value has its own grammar, one function each in `topos/wire`. An alphabet is members apart by `|`, with `\\|` and `\\\\` escaped, `not:` before them to forbid and `none` for no member at all. Fields are `key=value` members of an alphabet, parted at the first `=`. A scope is steps apart by `/`, every step kept. A region is `name@resolution`, its resolution digits or `*`. A requirement is `name@range`, parted at its last `@`, so a scoped name keeps its own. Each function reads its text and writes it back canonical, and what it writes reads back the same." at=place:topos by=lane-A epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/wire/values sig="ed25519:era1:DtrIjJ4m7qqyWfQPvSk28PKH45hnTwX9qhnH+e88q22ZQA6FLWGHf/K7tXP/xjkoX6PBpAT6DV6/LPX/tAWPDA==" value=lock
